3xmh|n|A witch, sorceress, or enchantress; also, a wizard. ; An ugly old woman. ; A fury; a she-monster. ; An eel-like marine marsipobranch (Myxine glutinosa), allied to the lamprey. It has a suctorial mouth, with labial appendages, and a single pair of gill openings. It is the type of the order Hyperotpeta. Called also hagfish, borer, slime eel, sucker, and sleepmarken. ; The hagdon or shearwater. ; An appearance of light and fire on a horse's mane or a man's hair. ; A small wood, or part of a wood or copse, which is marked off or inclosed for felling, or which has been felled. ; A quagmire; mossy ground where peat or turf has been cut.	a:4xbh,112,1;35hb,112,1;6c0r,95,114;10qd,79,1;5qb4,76,4;8ds8,70,9;3uj8,63,28;1ka0,56,4;6lfq,47,39;27ny,22,1~6c0r,95,114;6lfq,47,39;3uj8,63,28;8ds8,70,9;1ka0,56,4;5qb4,76,4;35hb,112,1;4xbh,112,1;10qd,79,1;27ny,22,1	v:8ds8,54,3~8ds8,54,3	V:1x30,139,1;1x2l,108,1;1sxm,67,3;66d4,36,7;9uib,31,2;3qrn,24,8;3t4j,7,4~3qrn,24,8;66d4,36,7;3t4j,7,4;1sxm,67,3;9uib,31,2;1x2l,108,1;1x30,139,1	n:35hb,145,10;e1u,144,2;4xbh,112,1;90fb,106,2;6c0r,100,161;8ds8,92,41;10qd,79,1;1ka0,52,3;1xju,44,2;3uj8,43,7;27ud,39,3;6lfq,14,4;dft,11,1~6c0r,100,161;8ds8,92,41;35hb,145,10;3uj8,43,7;6lfq,14,4;27ud,39,3;1ka0,52,3;90fb,106,2;1xju,44,2;e1u,144,2;dft,11,1;4xbh,112,1;10qd,79,1	N:1x30,155,3;1x2l,131,5;1x58,123,1;34uq,86,52;4bdu,58,13;5akw,50,6;5w3j,31,2;1gy2,15,1;4pwu,10,2;1993,6,4;7b8f,4,2~34uq,86,52;4bdu,58,13;5akw,50,6;1x2l,131,5;1993,6,4;1x30,155,3;4pwu,10,2;5w3j,31,2;7b8f,4,2;1x58,123,1;1gy2,15,1
