3z73|n|To agree in action, adaptation, or effect on the mind; to agree in sense or purport; as, the parts of a mechanism harmonize. ; To be in peace and friendship, as individuals, families, or public organizations. ; To agree in vocal or musical effect; to form a concord; as, the tones harmonize perfectly. ; To adjust in fit proportions; to cause to agree; to show the agreement of; to reconcile the apparent contradiction of. ; To accompany with harmony; to provide with parts, as an air, or melody.	N:6xk5,52,1~6xk5,52,1
