404d|v|To catch, or attempt to catch, birds by means of hawks trained for the purpose, and let loose on the prey; to practice falconry. ; To make an attack while on the wing; to soar and strike like a hawk; -- generally with at; as, to hawk at flies. ; To clear the throat with an audible sound by forcing an expiratory current of air through the narrow passage between the depressed soft palate and the root of the tongue, thus aiding in the removal of foreign substances. ; To raise by hawking, as phlegm. ; To offer for sale by outcry in the street; to carry (merchandise) about from place to place for sale; to peddle; as, to hawk goods or pamphlets.	o:5z5k,101,4;4xma,81,2;34uq,32,3;7f38,20,2;34wf,17,1;mkc,11,2~5z5k,101,4;34uq,32,3;7f38,20,2;mkc,11,2;4xma,81,2;34wf,17,1	s:1us0,121,3;69ck,86,13;9n0c,78,1;8z8e,77,1;9qdd,65,5;2q6i,49,1;89ag,44,2;76y2,31,2;7t8z,3,2~69ck,86,13;9qdd,65,5;1us0,121,3;76y2,31,2;89ag,44,2;7t8z,3,2;8z8e,77,1;9n0c,78,1;2q6i,49,1	D:5z4l,74,1~5z4l,74,1
